\n        \\\"last_updated_round\\\": 0,\\n        \\\"node_id\\\": \\\"root\\\",\\n        \\\"node_type\\\": \\\"root\\\",\\n        \\\"notes\\\": \\\"- 1) Problem classification: Dense causal self-attention prefill kernel (matrix-multiply-like + reduction + softmax). Outputs are output[b,t,h,d]; reductions over d for QK dot and over s for weighted V sum. Access is dense; no sparse/indirect indexing. Fixed small dims: num_q_heads=8, head_dim=128; variable dims: batch_size, seq_len; runtime branch on num_kv_heads in {1,8}.\\\\n- 2) Canonical math & dependencies: score(b,h,t,s)=sm_scale*dot(q[b,t,h,:],k[b,s,h,:]) for s<=t else -inf; p=softmax_s(score); out[b,t,h,:]=sum_s p*v[b,s,h,:]. Independent across (b,h,t) rows given shared K/V tensors. Streaming over s with online max/sum enables stable single-pass softmax accumulation.\\\\n- 3) Data layout & access: q/k/v/output in [B,S,H,D] BF16 with D likely contiguous. Dominant reads: K/V repeatedly across many t; Q read once per row tile. Dominant writes: output once. Reuse opportunities: stage K/V tiles in LDS, keep Q fragments and fp32 accumulators in registers.\\\\n- 4) Bottleneck regimes: (a) small S (<=~128): launch/latency and under-occupancy dominate; (b) medium S (~256-2048): balance between QK compute, softmax bookkeeping, and K/V bandwidth; (c) large S (>=~4096): O(S^2) work dominates, memory traffic and softmax-state management become primary limiters, especially if scores are materialized.\\\\n- 5) Kernel design space (knobs): mapping over (B,H,tile_t), tile sizes in t/s/d, hk specialization (1 vs 8), online vs materialized softmax path, fp32 accumulation policy, causal boundary handling, optional workspace usage, epilogue cast to BF16.\\\\n- 6) High-level skeleton: per (B,H,q-tile) load Q fragment -> iterate causal K/V tiles up to t-limit -> compute score fragments -> update softmax stats and output accumulators -> normalize -> store BF16 output. Synchronization points primarily around LDS K/V tile exchange.\\\\n- 7) Candidate kernel families (pruned): A) single-pass causal prefill (online normalization, no score workspace), B) materialized-score causal prefill (two-pass, easier debug but heavy traffic), C) partitioned-sequence causal prefill (split long S and merge partial softmax stats).\\\",\\n        \\\"overall_rating_0_to_10\\\": 6,\\n        \\\"parent_id\\\": null,\\n        \\\"solution_ref\\\": {\\n          \\\"eval\\\": {\\n            \\\"score\\\": null,\\n            \\\"score_name\\\": null,\\n            \\\"status\\\": \\\"not_evaluated\\\"\\n          },\\n          \\\"parent_solution_id\\\": null,\\n          \\\"solution_id\\\": null\\n        }\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \\\"action\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Implement a one-kernel causal prefill path that streams K/V tiles and performs numerically stable online softmax accumulation in FP32, with explicit handling for num_kv_heads=1 and 8.\\\",\\n          \\\"difficulty_1_to_5\\\": 4,\\n          \\\"expected_vs_baseline_factor\\\": 1.35,\\n          \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Avoids O(S^2) score/prob storage and should best match long-sequence dense prefill behavior on MI300X.\\\",\\n          \\\"score_0_to_1\\\": 0.74,\\n          \\\"title\\\": \\\"Prototype single-pass causal prefill kernel\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"choice\\\": \\\"family_single_pass\\\",\\n        \\\"confidence_0_to_1\\\": 0.66,\\n        \\\"decision\\\": \\\"open\\\",\\n        \\\"impacts\\\": {\\n          \\\"compute_intensity_and_hw_fit\\\": {\\n            \\\"hw_notes\\\": \\\"Maps well to MI300X when QK and PV fragments are tiled for high arithmetic reuse; wave64 and LDS usage must be balanced.\\\",\\n            \\\"notes\\\": \\\"Single-pass dataflow increases effective compute per byte by reusing staged K/V and avoiding global score writes.\\\",\\n            \\\"rating_0_to_10\\\": 8,\\n            \\\"risk\\\": \\\"If tile shapes are poor, MFMA utilization drops and occupancy can collapse.\\\"\\n          },\\n          \\\"memory_bandwidth\\\": {\\n            \\\"notes\\\": \\\"No score/prob materialization; global traffic mainly Q/K/V reads + output writes, favorable for medium/long S.\\\",\\n            \\\"rating_0_to_10\\\": 8,\\n            \\\"risk\\\": \\\"Still bandwidth-sensitive when hk=8 and batch is small.\\\"\\n          },\\n          \\\"register_pressure\\\": {\\n            \\\"notes\\\": \\\"Online softmax + D=128 output accumulators in FP32 can be register heavy.\\\",\\n            \\\"rating_0_to_10\\\": 4,\\n            \\\"risk\\\": \\\"High VGPR pressure may force low occupancy and spills.\\\"\\n          }\\n        },\\n        \\\"last_updated_round\\\": 0,\\n        \\\"node_id\\\": \\\"n1_single_pass\\\",\\n        \\\"node_type\\\": \\\"action\\\",\\n        \\\"notes\\\": \\\"Target regime: medium-to-large seq_len with minimal workspace. Includes explicit index path for hk=1 broadcast semantics instead of physical repeat_interleave.\\\\nSELF_CHECK: This sibling defines a no-workspace single-pass normalization contract; it cannot be combined in the same iteration with two-pass materialized-score or partition-merge contracts while preserving clear attribution.\\\",\\n        \\\"overall_rating_0_to_10\\\": 7,\\n        \\\"parent_id\\\": \\\"root\\\",\\n        \\\"solution_ref\\\": {\\n          \\\"eval\\\": {\\n            \\\"score\\\": null,\\n            \\\"score_name\\\": null,\\n            \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\"\\n          },\\n          \\\"parent_solution_id\\\": null,\\n          \\\"solution_id\\\": null\\n        }\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \\\"action\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Implement a two-pass causal prefill baseline that first computes/stores masked scores (or probabilities) then computes output with a second pass.\\\",\\n          \\\"difficulty_1_to_5\\\": 2,\\n          \\\"expected_vs_baseline_factor\\\": 0.85,\\n          \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Provides a simpler correctness/perf anchor and debugging reference despite expected memory overhead.\\\",\\n          \\\"score_0_to_1\\\": 0.48,\\n          \\\"title\\\": \\\"Prototype materialized-score causal prefill kernel\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"choice\\\": \\\"family_materialized_scores\\\",\\n        \\\"confidence_0_to_1\\\": 0.72,\\n        \\\"decision\\\": \\\"open\\\",\\n        \\\"impacts\\\": {\\n          \\\"compute_intensity_and_hw_fit\\\": {\\n            \\\"hw_notes\\\": \\\"Lower per-kernel complexity can improve implementation reliability but underuses MI300X potential for fused reuse.\\\",\\n            \\\"notes\\\": \\\"Extra global passes reduce effective compute intensity; easier to validate numerically.\\\",\\n            \\\"rating_0_to_10\\\": 5,\\n            \\\"risk\\\": \\\"May fail performance targets for long sequences due to quadratic workspace traffic.\\\"\\n          },\\n          \\\"memory_bandwidth\\\": {\\n            \\\"notes\\\": \\\"Writes/reads O(S^2) intermediate scores/probs; likely dominant bottleneck at moderate/large S.\\\",\\n            \\\"rating_0_to_10\\\": 2,\\n            \\\"risk\\\": \\\"Bandwidth and capacity pressure can be prohibitive on long-context prefill.\\\"\\n          },\\n          \\\"register_pressure\\\": {\\n            \\\"notes\\\": \\\"Lower on-chip state than online accumulation; simpler per-thread live ranges.\\\",\\n            \\\"rating_0_to_10\\\": 8,\\n            \\\"risk\\\": \\\"Benefit may be offset by synchronization and extra kernel launches.\\\"\\n          }\\n        },\\n        \\\"last_updated_round\\\": 0,\\n        \\\"node_id\\\": \\\"n2_materialized\\\",\\n        \\\"node_type\\\": \\\"action\\\",\\n        \\\"notes\\\": \\\"Target regime: short sequences and bring-up/testing. Good for validating masking/softmax/output correctness before deeper optimization.\\\\nSELF_CHECK: This sibling requires an intermediate workspace and two-pass contract, which is mutually exclusive with one-pass and partition-merge baselines for a single focused iteration.\\\",\\n        \\\"overall_rating_0_to_10\\\": 5,\\n        \\\"parent_id\\\": \\\"root\\\",\\n        \\\"solution_ref\\\": {\\n          \\\"eval\\\": {\\n            \\\"score\\\": null,\\n            \\\"score_name\\\": null,\\n            \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\"\\n          },\\n          \\\"parent_solution_id\\\": null,\\n          \\\"solution_id\\\": null\\n        }\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \\\"action\\\": {\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Implement a long-sequence-oriented kernel that partitions key/value sequence across cooperating blocks and merges partial softmax statistics/output contributions.\\\",\\n          \\\"difficulty_1_to_5\\\": 5,\\n          \\\"expected_vs_baseline_factor\\\": 1.2,\\n          \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Can raise parallelism and occupancy when seq_len is very large and single-block-per-row mapping underutilizes hardware.\\\",\\n          \\\"score_0_to_1\\\": 0.62,\\n          \\\"title\\\": \\\"Prototype partitioned-sequence causal prefill kernel\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"choice\\\": \\\"family_partitioned_sequence\\\",\\n        \\\"confidence_0_to_1\\\": 0.44,\\n        \\\"decision\\\": \\\"open\\\",\\n        \\\"impacts\\\": {\\n          \\\"compute_intensity_and_hw_fit\\\": {\\n            \\\"hw_notes\\\": \\\"Potentially better CU utilization on MI300X for very long S via more parallel work decomposition.\\\",\\n            \\\"notes\\\": \\\"Merge step adds overhead but can improve throughput when naive mapping has insufficient parallel rows.\\\",\\n            \\\"rating_0_to_10\\\": 7,\\n            \\\"risk\\\": \\\"Complex merge numerics and synchronization may erode gains.\\\"\\n          },\\n          \\\"memory_bandwidth\\\": {\\n            \\\"notes\\\": \\\"Avoids full score materialization, but extra partial-stat/output buffers add traffic versus pure single-pass.\\\",\\n            \\\"rating_0_to_10\\\": 6,\\n            \\\"risk\\\": \\\"Merge buffers may become bandwidth bottleneck if partition count is high.\\\"\\n          },\\n          \\\"register_pressure\\\": {\\n            \\\"notes\\\": \\\"Per-partition accumulators and merge metadata increase live state moderately.\\\",\\n            \\\"rating_0_to_10\\\": 5,\\n            \\\"risk\\\": \\\"Pressure and control complexity can reduce occupancy.\\\"\\n          }\\n        },\\n        \\\"last_updated_round\\\": 0,\\n        \\\"node_id\\\": \\\"n3_partitioned_sequence\\\",\\n        \\\"node_type\\\": \\\"action\\\",\\n        \\\"notes\\\": \\\"Target regime: very long seq_len where additional sequence-axis parallelism is needed. Prioritizes scalability over simplicity.\\\\nSELF_CHECK: This sibling introduces partition-merge semantics and buffer contracts that cannot be cleanly combined in the same first-iteration kernel with either single-pass row-stream or two-pass materialized-score baselines.\\\",\\n        \\\"overall_rating_0_to_10\\\": 6,\\n        \\\"parent_id\\\": \\\"root\\\",\\n        \\\"solution_ref\\\": {\\n          \\\"eval\\\": {\\n            \\\"score\\\": null,\\n            \\\"score_name\\\": null,\\n            \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\"\\n          },\\n          \\\"parent_solution_id\\\": null,\\n          \\\"solution_id\\\": null\\n        }\\n      }\\n    ],\\n    \\\"root_id\\\": \\\"root\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"kernel_summary\\\": \\\"This is dense causal self-attention prefill in HIP on MI300X with fixed Hq=8 and D=128 BF16 inputs, producing BF16 outputs via FP32 softmax math over sequence-length reductions; computation is O(B*H*S^2*D) with dense access, and the key structural branch is Hkv=8 (MHA) versus Hkv=1 (shared KV/GQA-style), which changes K/V reuse and indexing. Primary bottlenecks are expected to shift by regime: launch/occupancy for small S, mixed compute-memory balance for medium S, and quadratic traffic/softmax-state overhead for long S, making no-score-materialization single-pass causal dataflow the leading hypothesis while maintaining strict causal masking and numerical stability.\\\",\\n  \\\"open_questions\\\": [\\n    \\\"What are the production distributions of batch_size and seq_len (p50/p95/p99), and is performance priority short, medium, or very long contexts?\\\",\\n    \\\"Is contiguous layout guaranteed as [B,S,H,D] with D contiguous for q/k/v/output, or must arbitrary strides be supported?\\\",\\n    \\\"Can the runtime provide temporary workspace, and if so, what maximum size per batch is acceptable?\\\",\\n    \\\"What numerical error tolerance is required versus the PyTorch FP32-reference path (especially for long-sequence softmax accumulation)?\\\",\\n    \\\"How frequently does num_kv_heads=1 occur relative to 8, and should both paths be equally optimized or is one dominant?\\\",\\n    \\\"Are there constraints on deterministic reproducibility across runs/devices that would restrict reduction order choices?\\\",\\n    \\\"What are the exact integration expectations for host launch wrappers (ksearch_launch_* signatures, stream usage, and no-launch-in-main constraint) in the benchmark harness?\\\"\\n  ]\\n}\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"phase\": \"final_answer\",\n      \"role\": \"assistant\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"parallel_tool_calls\": true,\n  \"presence_penalty\": 0.0,\n  \"previous_response_id\": null,\n  \"prompt_cache_key\": null,\n  \"prompt_cache_retention\": null,\n  \"reasoning\": {\n    \"effort\": \"high\",\n    \"summary\": null\n  },\n  \"safety_identifier\": null,\n  \"service_tier\": \"default\",\n  \"store\": true,\n  \"temperature\": 1.0,\n  \"text\": {\n    \"format\": {\n      \"type\": \"text\"\n    },\n    \"verbosity\": \"medium\"\n  },\n  \"tool_choice\": \"auto\",\n  \"tools\": [],\n  \"top_logprobs\": 0,\n  \"top_p\": 0.98,\n  \"truncation\": \"disabled\",\n  \"usage\": {\n    \"input_tokens\": 2354,\n    \"input_tokens_details\": {\n      \"cached_tokens\": 0\n    },\n    \"outp